  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan: Population Movement, 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance is focused on Afghanistan&#x2019;s border provinces and urban centers, especially:

Torkham, Spin Boldak, Ghulam Khan, Badini (border points)

Provinces like Nangarhar, Kandahar, Khost, Helmand, Herat, and Kabul</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the mass return of Afghans from Pakistan and Iran, the Afghan Red Crescent Society, with IFRC support, aims to assist 525,000 vulnerable people through a 24-month operation. We will provide emergency aid&#x2014;shelter, healthcare, food, and cash&#x2014;while supporting long-term recovery, livelihoods, and reintegration. With a focus on dignity, protection, and inclusion, the strategy ensures coordinated, people-centered support at borders and in communities, helping returnees rebuild their lives with safety and hope.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation targets 525,000 people, prioritizing:

Returnees from Pakistan and Iran

Vulnerable groups such as women, unaccompanied children, elderly, disabled people, and those facing extreme poverty

Host communities struggling with the added pressure</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The strategy lays out a 24-month, phased response plan led by the Afghan Red Crescent Society (ARCS) with support from the IFRC and partners. It includes:

Emergency aid (shelter, food, WASH, healthcare, cash assistance)

Recovery and reintegration efforts (livelihoods, legal support, education)

Coordination with local/international stakeholders

Special attention to protection, mental health, and gender inclusion

Key operational elements involve mobile health teams, transitional shelters, vocational training, community health education, and legal documentation support.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This emergency operation was launched in response to the mass return and deportation of Afghan nationals from Pakistan and Iran following government repatriation policies (notably Pakistan&apos;s Illegal Foreigners Repatriation Plan - IFRP). The return of nearly one million Afghans since September 2023 has overwhelmed Afghanistan&#x2019;s already fragile infrastructure, worsening humanitarian conditions, especially for vulnerable populations.</narrative>
  </description>
